# BIFROST ENGINE LICENSE SELECTION AGREEMENT (LSA)

Version 1.0

Copyright © Calvin Vandenberg CD ("Armscream") All Rights Reserved.

## 1. Purpose

This License Selection Agreement ("LSA") governs access to and use of the Bifrost Engine ("Engine").

Any person or entity obtaining, using, modifying, compiling, distributing, or creating works based upon the Engine must elect and comply with exactly one of the following licenses for each Project:

1. Commercial Engine License ("CEL")
2. Open Community Game License ("OCGL")

No Project may simultaneously operate under both licenses.

## 2. Definitions

### 2.1 Engine

"Engine" means the Bifrost Engine software, source code, tools, libraries, build systems, documentation, examples, official plugins, official extensions, and all associated materials distributed by the Engine Publisher.

### 2.2 Engine Publisher

"Engine Publisher" means Calvin Vandenberg C.D., successors, assigns, or any entity designated by the Engine Publisher.

### 2.3 Project

"Project" means any game, application, simulation, tool, product, or derivative work developed using any portion of the Engine.

### 2.4 Public Release

"Public Release" means any distribution of a Project to any person outside the development team, including:

* Alpha releases
* Beta releases
* Early Access releases
* Demonstrations
* Public test builds
* Commercial releases
* Free releases

### 2.5 Patch

"Patch" means instructions, diffs, source modifications, or transformation data necessary to modify an official Engine release.

A Patch must not constitute a complete or substantially complete redistribution of Engine Source Code.

### 2.6 Plugin

"Plugin" means software that extends Engine functionality through published APIs without modifying Engine Source Code.

### 2.7 Extension

"Extension" means software that extends Engine functionality and may require Engine Patches to operate.

### 2.8 Fork

"Fork" means any redistributed version of the Engine containing modified Engine Source Code.

## 3. License Election

Prior to any Public Release, the Project owner must elect either:

A. Commercial Engine License (CEL)

or

B. Open Community Game License (OCGL)

The selected license governs the entire Project.

## 4. Irrevocability of Election

Projects released under the OCGL may not subsequently be relicensed under the CEL or any other license permitting commercialization.

Projects released under the CEL may not subsequently claim OCGL status for prior proprietary releases.

## 5. Single Canonical Engine

The Engine Publisher maintains the sole official Engine distribution.

Users may:

* Create Plugins and distribute them.
* Create Extensions and distribute them.
* Create Patches and distribute them.
* Submit Contributions.

Users may not:

* Publish Forks.
* Redistribute modified Engine Source Code.
* Distribute alternative Engine distributions.

## 6. Contributions

Contributors retain ownership of their Contributions.

By submitting a Contribution to the Engine, the Contributor grants the Engine Publisher a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:

* Use
* Modify
* Reproduce
* Distribute
* Sublicense
* Relicense
* Incorporate

the Contribution into the Engine and any future version of the Engine.

Contributors may continue to use, license, sell, distribute, or otherwise exploit their Contributions outside of the Engine under any terms they choose.

Contributions may not be withdrawn after acceptance.

Submission of a Contribution grants no governance, ownership, veto, approval, or control rights over the Engine.

## 7. Attribution

All Projects developed using the Engine shall display:

1. The official Bifrost Engine logo during startup.
2. A copyright notice identifying the Engine.
3. Attribution in Project credits.

Specific attribution requirements are defined in the selected license.

## 8. Reservation of Rights

All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Engine Publisher.

The Engine Publisher retains the unrestricted right to:

* Relicense the Engine.
* Offer custom licenses.
* Grant exceptions.
* Enter commercial agreements.
* Modify future license versions.

## 9. Acceptance

By obtaining, using, modifying, compiling, or distributing the Engine, the User agrees to the terms of this Agreement and the selected governing license.

